1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,675
You've reread the moles chapter twice,

2
00:00:02,675 --> 00:00:05,841
and you still can't tell if it stuck.

3
00:00:05,841 --> 00:00:08,215
A textbook never quizzes you back.

4
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:15,449
OmniSTEM fixes that: a Duolingo-style AP Chemistry app with

5
00:00:15,449 --> 00:00:18,226
short lessons, hearts, XP,

6
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:22,392
streaks, and a daily equation-balancing puzzle.

7
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,155
On the landing page,

8
00:00:25,155 --> 00:00:28,227
a student sees bite-size AP Chemistry lessons,

9
00:00:28,227 --> 00:00:29,983
a daily equation-balancing puzzle,

10
00:00:29,983 --> 00:00:32,177
and a streak to keep.

11
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:35,181
The welcome screen sets expectations:

12
00:00:35,181 --> 00:00:37,919
daily two-minute lessons and a puzzle,

13
00:00:37,919 --> 00:00:39,744
so practice stays short.

14
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:42,524
Get started asks one question,

15
00:00:42,524 --> 00:00:44,144
what brings you here,

16
00:00:44,144 --> 00:00:46,573
with AP Chem, high school chem,

17
00:00:46,573 --> 00:00:48,598
or just exploring as choices.

18
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:52,144
Clicking AP Chem outlines the card in red and

19
00:00:52,144 --> 00:00:54,987
enables Continue, so the app can match its tone

20
00:00:54,987 --> 00:00:55,935
to the student.

21
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,564
It's built on Next.js,

22
00:00:58,564 --> 00:01:02,293
with a Zustand store that syncs to Supabase,

23
00:01:02,293 --> 00:01:05,090
or to local storage without it.

24
00:01:05,090 --> 00:01:06,955
GPT-4o writes the questions,

25
00:01:06,955 --> 00:01:11,616
zod checks them, and a seed bank is the fallback.

26
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:17,851
Try it at github.com/Mallard64/stemduolingo.
